        {
          "id": "b7be3303-eb84-4e43-b90b-3e417803dd00",
          "kind": "activity",
          "title": "OPTION — Ski touring at Rogers Pass (guided)",
          "status": "planned",
          "order": 1,
          "location": "Rogers Pass",
          "mapsQuery": "Rogers Pass Discovery Centre, Glacier National Park, BC",
          "description": "Spontaneous idea from the Rogers Pass guide — **45 min from Revelstoke**, right on our Banff→Revelstoke / Revelstoke→Golden loop. A perfect flex-day use before the heli block.\n\n**What:** guided intro day at Rogers Pass (Glacier National Park) — ancient forests, alpine bowls & couloirs. Terrain is *advanced/expert* with big climbs, so we go with an **ACMG-certified guide** (mixed ski/splitboard OK — Niko on splitboard).\n\n**Logistics:** ~65 km from Revelstoke via Trans-Canada (Hwy 1). Park at Rogers Pass Discovery Centre / dedicated winter lots. Same road that carries the avalanche artillery — respect closures.\n\n**Be ready for:**\n- **Winter Permit mandatory** (all zones since 2026, even \"unrestricted\") — daily permit only at Summit Station or annual online\n- **Parks Canada pass** required\n- **Avalanche bulletin** (avalanche.ca) + **Rogers Pass interactive map** status (updated ~07:00, lots closed until then) — check before driving\n- Full touring kit: splitboard + skins / skis + skins, beacon/probe/shovel (+ airbag as for heli)\n\nDecide with the guide the morning-of based on avy hazard & what's open. *Alternative:* keep the RMR lift day — this block is the \"decide-on-the-hill\" option.",
          "links": [
            {
